# Netlify syntax.
#
# The chart lives at /ipa-chart (Netlify resolves that to ipa-chart.html), which
# is what the canonical tag, the sitemap and every internal link now say. These
# are memorable aliases onto it, not copies: two near-identical pages would
# compete with each other in search and neither would rank.
#
# There is deliberately no rule for /ipa-chart itself — it is the destination,
# and a rule pointing it at itself would loop.
/ipa-keyboard      /ipa-chart   301
/ipa-keyboard/     /ipa-chart   301
/ipa-chart/        /ipa-chart   301
/ipa               /ipa-chart   301

# Same arrangement for the dictionary: /dictionary is the page (Netlify serves
# dictionary.html for it), and these are aliases onto it rather than copies.
/dictionary/       /dictionary  301
/dict              /dictionary  301
/etymology         /dictionary  301
